('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000198','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which heat-transfer mechanism involves bulk movement of a fluid?','["Conduction", "Convection", "Radiation", "Reflection"]','"Convection"','Convection transfers heat through moving liquid or gas.','Wikipedia: Convection','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convection','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000199','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which heat-transfer mechanism can operate through a vacuum?','["Conduction", "Liquid convection", "Radiation", "Gas convection"]','"Radiation"','Electromagnetic radiation can carry energy through empty space.','Wikipedia: Thermal radiation','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_radiation','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000200','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is density?','["Force per unit area", "Energy per unit time", "Distance per unit time", "Mass per unit volume"]','"Mass per unit volume"','Density is mass divided by volume.','Wikipedia: Density','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Density','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000201','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which state of matter has a definite volume but ordinarily takes its container''s shape?','["Liquid", "Solid", "Gas", "Plasma"]','"Liquid"','Liquids have nearly fixed volume while flowing to fit a container.','Wikipedia: Liquid','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liquid','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000202','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which state of matter contains many freely moving ions and electrons?','["Liquid", "Plasma", "Solid", "Supercritical liquid only"]','"Plasma"','Plasma is an ionized state with charged particles.','Wikipedia: Plasma (physics)','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plasma_%28physics%29','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000203','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is an isotope?','["Different elements with equal mass", "Molecules with no electrons", "Atoms of one element with different neutron counts", "Atoms with different proton counts"]','"Atoms of one element with different neutron counts"','Isotopes have the same proton count but different numbers of neutrons.','Wikipedia: Isotope','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isotope','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000204','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is an ion?','["An atom with no neutrons", "A neutral gas only", "A photon", "An atom or molecule with a net electric charge"]','"An atom or molecule with a net electric charge"','Ions have gained or lost electrons and carry a net charge.','Wikipedia: Ion','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ion','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000205','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is a covalent bond?','["A bond involving shared electrons", "A bond made only by gravity", "A bond with no electrons", "A purely magnetic attraction"]','"A bond involving shared electrons"','Covalent bonds form when atoms share electron pairs.','Wikipedia: Covalent bond','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Covalent_bond','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000206','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is an ionic bond chiefly based on?','["Shared protons", "Electrostatic attraction between opposite ions", "Gravitational attraction", "Nuclear fusion"]','"Electrostatic attraction between opposite ions"','Oppositely charged ions attract through electrostatic forces.','Wikipedia: Ionic bonding','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionic_bonding','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000207','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is an oxidation reaction in terms of electron transfer?','["Gain of electrons", "Gain of neutrons", "Loss of electrons", "Loss of protons"]','"Loss of electrons"','Oxidation involves loss of electrons, while reduction involves gain.','Wikipedia: Redox','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redox','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000208','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is reduction in terms of electron transfer?','["Loss of electrons", "Gain of protons", "Loss of neutrons", "Gain of electrons"]','"Gain of electrons"','Reduction involves gain of electrons.','Wikipedia: Redox','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redox','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000209','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which mixture has a solute dissolved uniformly in a solvent?','["Solution", "Suspension", "Coarse emulsion", "Sediment"]','"Solution"','A solution is a homogeneous mixture of dissolved solute and solvent.','Wikipedia: Solution (chemistry)','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solution_%28chemistry%29','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000210','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What does filtration separate from a fluid?','["Dissolved salt completely", "Undissolved particles", "Individual atoms", "Electric charge"]','"Undissolved particles"','Filtration captures particles too large to pass through a filter''s pores.','Wikipedia: Filtration','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filtration','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000211','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which separation process relies on differences in boiling behavior?','["Filtration", "Sieving", "Distillation", "Magnetic separation"]','"Distillation"','Distillation separates components through vaporization and condensation.','Wikipedia: Distillation','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distillation','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000212','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the chemical formula for water?','["CO2", "O2", "NaCl", "H2O"]','"H2O"','A water molecule contains two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.','Wikipedia: Water','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000213','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the chemical formula for carbon dioxide?','["CO2", "CO", "CH4", "H2O"]','"CO2"','Carbon dioxide contains one carbon atom and two oxygen atoms.','Wikipedia: Carbon dioxide','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_dioxide','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000214','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the chemical formula for methane?','["CO2", "CH4", "NH3", "H2O"]','"CH4"','Methane contains one carbon atom bonded to four hydrogen atoms.','Wikipedia: Methane','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methane','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000215','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the chemical formula for sodium chloride?','["KCl", "NaOH", "NaCl", "CaCO3"]','"NaCl"','Common salt is sodium chloride, represented as NaCl.','Wikipedia: Sodium chloride','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_chloride','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000216','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the chemical formula for ammonia?','["NO2", "N2O", "CH4", "NH3"]','"NH3"','Ammonia consists of one nitrogen atom and three hydrogen atoms.','Wikipedia: Ammonia','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ammonia','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000217','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which macromolecules act as most biological enzymes?','["Proteins", "Lipids only", "Sugars only", "Mineral salts"]','"Proteins"','Most enzymes are proteins, though some RNA molecules also act as catalysts.','Wikipedia: Enzyme','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enzyme','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000218','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the basic structural unit of living organisms?','["Atom only", "Cell", "Organ", "Chromosome"]','"Cell"','Cells are the basic structural and functional units of life.','Wikipedia: Cell (biology)','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cell_%28biology%29','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000219','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which cell structure selectively controls movement into and out of a cell?','["Ribosome", "Nucleolus", "Cell membrane", "Chromosome"]','"Cell membrane"','The cell membrane regulates exchange between a cell and its environment.','Wikipedia: Cell membrane','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cell_membrane','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000220','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which plant-cell organelle contains chlorophyll?','["Mitochondrion", "Lysosome", "Ribosome", "Chloroplast"]','"Chloroplast"','Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll and perform photosynthesis.','Wikipedia: Chloroplast','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chloroplast','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000221','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which process produces genetically identical daughter cells in ordinary cell division?','["Mitosis", "Meiosis", "Fertilization", "Mutation"]','"Mitosis"','Mitosis distributes duplicated chromosomes into genetically matching nuclei.','Wikipedia: Mitosis','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mitosis','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000222','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which process reduces the chromosome number to form gametes?','["Mitosis", "Meiosis", "Binary fission", "Translation"]','"Meiosis"','Meiosis halves the chromosome number during sexual reproduction.','Wikipedia: Meiosis','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meiosis','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000223','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is osmosis?','["Movement of light through glass", "Division of a nucleus", "Movement of water through a selectively permeable membrane", "Breakdown of proteins"]','"Movement of water through a selectively permeable membrane"','Osmosis is water movement across a selectively permeable membrane driven by differences in water potential.','Wikipedia: Osmosis','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osmosis','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000224','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is diffusion?','["Flow only against a concentration gradient", "Cell division", "Protein assembly", "Net movement from higher to lower concentration"]','"Net movement from higher to lower concentration"','Diffusion causes particles to spread from higher to lower concentration.','Wikipedia: Diffusion','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diffusion','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000225','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which human organ pumps blood through the circulatory system?','["Heart", "Liver", "Kidney", "Pancreas"]','"Heart"','The heart generates pressure to circulate blood.','Wikipedia: Heart','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000226','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which human organs exchange oxygen and carbon dioxide with inhaled air?','["Kidneys", "Lungs", "Stomach", "Liver"]','"Lungs"','Gas exchange occurs primarily across alveoli in the lungs.','Wikipedia: Lung','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lung','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000227','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which human organs filter blood to form urine?','["Lungs", "Pancreas", "Kidneys", "Spleen"]','"Kidneys"','The kidneys regulate blood composition and remove wastes in urine.','Wikipedia: Kidney','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidney','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000228','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which organ produces bile?','["Stomach", "Kidney", "Spleen", "Liver"]','"Liver"','The liver produces bile, which aids fat digestion.','Wikipedia: Liver','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liver','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000229','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which small organ stores and concentrates bile?','["Gallbladder", "Pancreas", "Appendix", "Spleen"]','"Gallbladder"','The gallbladder stores and concentrates bile from the liver.','Wikipedia: Gallbladder','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gallbladder','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000230','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which organ produces the hormones insulin and glucagon?','["Spleen", "Pancreas", "Thyroid", "Gallbladder"]','"Pancreas"','Pancreatic islet cells produce insulin and glucagon to regulate blood glucose.','Wikipedia: Pancreas','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pancreas','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000231','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which hormone lowers blood glucose by promoting cellular uptake and storage?','["Glucagon", "Adrenaline", "Insulin", "Melatonin"]','"Insulin"','Insulin helps lower circulating glucose through uptake and storage.','Wikipedia: Insulin','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insulin','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000232','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which hormone helps raise blood glucose when it falls too low?','["Insulin", "Melatonin", "Oxytocin", "Glucagon"]','"Glucagon"','Glucagon promotes glucose release, including from liver glycogen.','Wikipedia: Glucagon','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glucagon','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000233','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which digestive enzyme begins starch breakdown in the mouth?','["Amylase", "Pepsin", "Lipase", "Trypsin"]','"Amylase"','Salivary amylase begins breaking starch into smaller carbohydrates.','Wikipedia: Amylase','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amylase','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000234','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which part of the digestive tract absorbs most nutrients?','["Esophagus", "Small intestine", "Large intestine", "Stomach"]','"Small intestine"','Most nutrient absorption occurs in the small intestine.','Wikipedia: Small intestine','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Small_intestine','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000235','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which tube carries food from the mouth toward the stomach?','["Trachea", "Aorta", "Esophagus", "Ureter"]','"Esophagus"','The esophagus moves swallowed food to the stomach.','Wikipedia: Esophagus','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Esophagus','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000236','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which tube carries air from the throat toward the lungs?','["Esophagus", "Ureter", "Aorta", "Trachea"]','"Trachea"','The trachea is the windpipe that conducts air toward the bronchi.','Wikipedia: Trachea','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trachea','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000237','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which part of the brain coordinates movement and balance?','["Cerebellum", "Hypothalamus", "Medulla only", "Pituitary gland"]','"Cerebellum"','The cerebellum is important for coordinated movement and balance.','Wikipedia: Cerebellum','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerebellum','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000238','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which brain structure helps regulate body temperature and hunger?','["Cerebellum", "Hypothalamus", "Corpus callosum", "Occipital cortex"]','"Hypothalamus"','The hypothalamus regulates many homeostatic functions including temperature and hunger.','Wikipedia: Hypothalamus','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypothalamus','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000239','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which type of neuron carries signals toward the central nervous system?','["Motor neuron", "Interneuron only", "Sensory neuron", "Muscle fiber"]','"Sensory neuron"','Sensory neurons carry information from receptors toward the central nervous system.','Wikipedia: Sensory neuron','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sensory_neuron','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000240','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which mineral is especially important in the structure of bones and teeth?','["Sodium", "Potassium", "Iodine", "Calcium"]','"Calcium"','Calcium compounds help give bones and teeth their mineral strength.','Wikipedia: Calcium','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calcium','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000241','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which vitamin deficiency causes scurvy?','["Vitamin C", "Vitamin D", "Vitamin B12", "Vitamin K"]','"Vitamin C"','Scurvy results from inadequate vitamin C.','Wikipedia: Scurvy','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scurvy','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000242','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which vitamin deficiency can cause rickets in children?','["Vitamin C", "Vitamin D", "Vitamin B1", "Vitamin B12"]','"Vitamin D"','Vitamin D deficiency can impair bone mineralization and cause rickets.','Wikipedia: Rickets','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rickets','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000243','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which vitamin is important for normal blood clotting?','["Vitamin C", "Vitamin B12", "Vitamin K", "Vitamin A"]','"Vitamin K"','Vitamin K is needed to produce several normal clotting factors.','Wikipedia: Vitamin K','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitamin_K','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000244','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which gland produces thyroid hormones?','["Pituitary only", "Adrenal", "Pineal", "Thyroid"]','"Thyroid"','Thyroid hormones are produced by the thyroid gland in the neck.','Wikipedia: Thyroid','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thyroid','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000245','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which hormone is strongly associated with the sleep-wake cycle?','["Melatonin", "Insulin", "Glucagon", "Thyroxine"]','"Melatonin"','Melatonin secretion helps signal nighttime and regulate circadian timing.','Wikipedia: Melatonin','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melatonin','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000246','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which joint connects the upper arm to the forearm?','["Shoulder", "Elbow", "Wrist", "Hip"]','"Elbow"','The elbow joins the humerus with the radius and ulna.','Wikipedia: Elbow','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbow','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000247','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which bone is commonly called the thighbone?','["Tibia", "Fibula", "Femur", "Humerus"]','"Femur"','The femur is the bone of the thigh.','Wikipedia: Femur','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Femur','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000248','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which bone is commonly called the kneecap?','["Scapula", "Clavicle", "Sternum", "Patella"]','"Patella"','The patella lies at the front of the knee joint.','Wikipedia: Patella','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patella','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000249','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which bone is commonly called the collarbone?','["Clavicle", "Scapula", "Sternum", "Pelvis"]','"Clavicle"','The clavicle connects the sternum to the shoulder region.','Wikipedia: Clavicle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clavicle','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000250','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which bone is commonly called the shoulder blade?','["Clavicle", "Scapula", "Humerus", "Ulna"]','"Scapula"','The scapula is the flat bone at the back of the shoulder.','Wikipedia: Scapula','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scapula','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000251','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which layer of Earth lies between the crust and core?','["Atmosphere", "Lithosphere only", "Mantle", "Hydrosphere"]','"Mantle"','The mantle extends from below the crust to the outer core.','Wikipedia: Mantle (geology)','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mantle_%28geology%29','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000252','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which Earth layer is mainly liquid iron alloy?','["Crust", "Inner core", "Upper mantle", "Outer core"]','"Outer core"','Earth''s outer core is liquid and surrounds its solid inner core.','Wikipedia: Earth''s outer core','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth%27s_outer_core','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000253','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which process breaks rock down in place?','["Weathering", "Erosion", "Deposition", "Subduction"]','"Weathering"','Weathering breaks down rock without requiring its transport elsewhere.','Wikipedia: Weathering','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weathering','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000254','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which process moves weathered material from one location to another?','["Crystallization", "Erosion", "Metamorphism", "Solidification"]','"Erosion"','Erosion removes and transports rock, soil or sediment.','Wikipedia: Erosion','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erosion','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000255','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which type of rock forms when molten material cools and solidifies?','["Sedimentary rock", "Metamorphic rock", "Igneous rock", "Fossil fuel"]','"Igneous rock"','Igneous rocks form from cooling magma or lava.','Wikipedia: Igneous rock','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igneous_rock','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000256','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which type of rock forms when existing rock changes under heat and pressure without melting?','["Igneous rock", "Unconsolidated sediment", "Volcanic glass only", "Metamorphic rock"]','"Metamorphic rock"','Metamorphic rocks develop through solid-state changes caused by heat, pressure and fluids.','Wikipedia: Metamorphic rock','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metamorphic_rock','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000257','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which sedimentary rock is commonly made mostly of calcium carbonate?','["Limestone", "Granite", "Basalt", "Slate"]','"Limestone"','Limestone is primarily composed of calcium-carbonate minerals.','Wikipedia: Limestone','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limestone','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000258','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which metamorphic rock forms from limestone?','["Slate", "Marble", "Quartzite", "Gneiss only"]','"Marble"','Limestone can recrystallize under metamorphism to form marble.','Wikipedia: Marble','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marble','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000259','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which metamorphic rock commonly forms from shale?','["Marble", "Quartzite", "Slate", "Basalt"]','"Slate"','Slate forms through low-grade metamorphism of shale and related fine-grained rocks.','Wikipedia: Slate','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slate','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000260','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is magma called after it reaches Earth''s surface?','["Basalt only", "Ash", "Obsidian only", "Lava"]','"Lava"','Molten rock is called lava when it emerges at the surface.','Wikipedia: Lava','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lava','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000261','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which boundary involves one tectonic plate sinking beneath another?','["Subduction zone", "Transform boundary only", "Mid-ocean ridge only", "Continental rift only"]','"Subduction zone"','Subduction occurs when one plate descends beneath another into the mantle.','Wikipedia: Subduction','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subduction','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000262','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which boundary commonly creates new oceanic crust?','["Transform boundary", "Divergent boundary", "Collision zone only", "Subduction zone only"]','"Divergent boundary"','New oceanic crust forms as plates separate at mid-ocean ridges.','Wikipedia: Divergent boundary','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divergent_boundary','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000263','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which instrument records seismic waves?','["Barometer", "Anemometer", "Seismometer", "Hygrometer"]','"Seismometer"','Seismometers detect ground motion produced by seismic waves.','Wikipedia: Seismometer','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seismometer','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000264','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which type of seismic wave cannot travel through liquid?','["P wave", "Sound wave", "Pressure wave", "S wave"]','"S wave"','S waves are shear waves, and liquids cannot support shear rigidity.','Wikipedia: S wave','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S_wave','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000265','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which cloud type is strongly associated with thunderstorms?','["Cumulonimbus", "Cirrus", "Stratus", "Altostratus"]','"Cumulonimbus"','Cumulonimbus clouds develop vertically and produce thunderstorms.','Wikipedia: Cumulonimbus cloud','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumulonimbus_cloud','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000266','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the water cycle process in which plants release water vapor through leaves?','["Condensation", "Transpiration", "Infiltration", "Precipitation"]','"Transpiration"','Transpiration releases water vapor from plant surfaces, mainly leaves.','Wikipedia: Transpiration','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transpiration','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000267','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the point at which air becomes saturated when cooled at constant pressure called?','["Boiling point", "Freezing point", "Dew point", "Flash point"]','"Dew point"','The dew point is the temperature at which water vapor reaches saturation under specified conditions.','Wikipedia: Dew point','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dew_point','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000268','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which atmosphere layer contains most ordinary weather?','["Mesosphere", "Thermosphere", "Exosphere", "Troposphere"]','"Troposphere"','Most weather occurs in the troposphere, the lowest atmospheric layer.','Wikipedia: Troposphere','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troposphere','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000269','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which atmosphere layer contains most of the ozone layer?','["Stratosphere", "Troposphere", "Mesosphere", "Exosphere"]','"Stratosphere"','Most atmospheric ozone is concentrated in the stratosphere.','Wikipedia: Ozone layer','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ozone_layer','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000270','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which phenomenon is caused by charged particles interacting with Earth''s upper atmosphere?','["Rainbow", "Aurora", "Mirage", "Halo only"]','"Aurora"','Auroras occur when energetic charged particles excite atmospheric gases.','Wikipedia: Aurora','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aurora','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000271','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which optical phenomenon occurs when sunlight is refracted, reflected and dispersed by water droplets?','["Aurora", "Mirage", "Rainbow", "Solar flare"]','"Rainbow"','Water droplets bend, reflect and disperse sunlight to form rainbows.','Wikipedia: Rainbow','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000272','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the study of weather and the atmosphere called?','["Geology", "Seismology", "Limnology", "Meteorology"]','"Meteorology"','Meteorology studies atmospheric processes and weather.','Wikipedia: Meteorology','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meteorology','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000273','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is the study of inland waters called?','["Limnology", "Meteorology", "Astronomy", "Volcanology"]','"Limnology"','Limnology studies lakes, rivers and other inland waters.','Wikipedia: Limnology','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limnology','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000274','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which kind of celestial object is primarily a small icy body that can form a tail near the Sun?','["Asteroid", "Comet", "Planet", "Neutron star"]','"Comet"','A comet releases gas and dust as its ices warm near the Sun, sometimes forming tails.','Wikipedia: Comet','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comet','science',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-060000000275','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What is a meteoroid called while producing a bright streak in the atmosphere?','["Meteorite", "Comet", "Meteor", "Asteroid belt"]','"Meteor"','The light phenomenon produced by an entering meteoroid is called a meteor.','Wikipedia: Meteoroid','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meteoroid','science',60)
