('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000229','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which seaweed is commonly used for Japanese dashi?','["Kombu", "Nori", "Sea lettuce", "Dulse"]','"Kombu"','Kombu kelp is a common ingredient in Japanese dashi broth.','Wikipedia: Dashi','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dashi','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000230','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which ingredient is responsible for capsaicin heat in food?','["Black pepper", "Chili pepper", "Ginger", "Cinnamon"]','"Chili pepper"','Capsaicin is the main pungent compound in chili peppers.','Wikipedia: Capsaicin','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capsaicin','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000231','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which spice is obtained from the dried flower buds of a tree?','["Nutmeg", "Cumin", "Clove", "Cardamom"]','"Clove"','Cloves are dried flower buds of the clove tree.','Wikipedia: Clove','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clove','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000232','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which spice is the seed inside the fruit that also supplies mace?','["Clove", "Saffron", "Anise", "Nutmeg"]','"Nutmeg"','Nutmeg is the seed, while mace is the surrounding aril.','Wikipedia: Nutmeg','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutmeg','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000233','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which spice comes from the aril around a nutmeg seed?','["Mace", "Clove", "Turmeric", "Fenugreek"]','"Mace"','Mace is the lacy seed covering of the nutmeg fruit.','Wikipedia: Mace (spice)','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mace_%28spice%29','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000234','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which spice gives many curries a bright yellow color?','["Cumin", "Turmeric", "Clove", "Cardamom"]','"Turmeric"','Turmeric contains yellow curcuminoid pigments.','Wikipedia: Turmeric','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turmeric','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000235','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which spice is produced by drying and grinding sweet or mild peppers?','["Cinnamon", "Coriander", "Paprika", "Allspice"]','"Paprika"','Paprika is made from dried peppers, with varieties differing in heat and smokiness.','Wikipedia: Paprika','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paprika','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000236','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which spice comes from berries of the Pimenta dioica tree?','["Clove", "Anise", "Cumin", "Allspice"]','"Allspice"','Allspice is the dried unripe berry of Pimenta dioica.','Wikipedia: Allspice','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allspice','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000237','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which herb is also called cilantro in American English?','["Coriander leaf", "Parsley", "Basil", "Rosemary"]','"Coriander leaf"','Cilantro refers to the leaves of the coriander plant in American English.','Wikipedia: Coriander','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coriander','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000238','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which herb has needle-like leaves and is often paired with roast lamb?','["Basil", "Rosemary", "Cilantro", "Chervil"]','"Rosemary"','Rosemary has aromatic needle-like leaves and is a common seasoning for roasted meats.','Wikipedia: Rosemary','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosemary','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000239','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which herb gives classic béarnaise sauce its anise-like flavor?','["Basil", "Oregano", "Tarragon", "Mint"]','"Tarragon"','Béarnaise traditionally contains tarragon, shallots and vinegar in an egg-and-butter sauce.','Wikipedia: Béarnaise sauce','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%A9arnaise_sauce','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000240','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which seed gives anise its licorice-like flavor?','["Cumin seed", "Mustard seed", "Sesame seed", "Anise seed"]','"Anise seed"','Anise seeds contain anethole, which produces a licorice-like aroma.','Wikipedia: Anise','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anise','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000241','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which leafy plant is the source of ordinary black and green tea?','["Camellia sinensis", "Coffea arabica", "Mentha spicata", "Hibiscus sabdariffa"]','"Camellia sinensis"','Black and green teas both come from Camellia sinensis, processed differently.','Wikipedia: Tea','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000242','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which coffee species is commonly known as arabica?','["Camellia sinensis", "Coffea arabica", "Theobroma cacao", "Vanilla planifolia"]','"Coffea arabica"','Arabica coffee comes from Coffea arabica.','Wikipedia: Coffea arabica','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffea_arabica','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000243','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What ingredient is the basis of traditional aioli in its simplest form?','["Tomato", "Basil", "Garlic", "Cheese"]','"Garlic"','Traditional aioli is an emulsion based on garlic and oil; some versions include egg.','Wikipedia: Aioli','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aioli','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000244','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What gives squid-ink pasta its dark color?','["Cocoa", "Activated yeast", "Coffee grounds", "Squid ink"]','"Squid ink"','Squid ink provides both dark pigment and marine flavor.','Wikipedia: Squid ink','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squid_ink','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000245','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What gives beetroot its red-purple color?','["Betalain pigments", "Chlorophyll", "Melanin", "Hemoglobin"]','"Betalain pigments"','Beetroot contains betalains, including red-violet betacyanins.','Wikipedia: Betalain','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betalain','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000246','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which ingredient thickens a traditional roux?','["Yeast", "Flour", "Vinegar", "Salt"]','"Flour"','A roux is cooked flour and fat used to thicken sauces and soups.','Wikipedia: Roux','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roux','food',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8000-030000000247','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','What ingredient provides the base for traditional hollandaise?','["Tomato and onion", "Cream and flour", "Egg yolk and butter", "Yogurt and cucumber"]','"Egg yolk and butter"','Hollandaise is an emulsion of egg yolk and butter, typically flavored with lemon juice.','Wikipedia: Hollandaise sauce','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollandaise_sauce','food',60),
