('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000004','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal has defensive spines that are modified hairs?','["Koala", "Echidna", "Horseshoe crab", "Parrotfish"]','"Echidna"','Echidna spines are specialized hairs, not detachable quills.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Echidna','https://www.britannica.com/animal/echidna','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000005','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal catches ants or termites with a long sticky tongue?','["Echidna", "Horseshoe crab", "Parrotfish", "Koala"]','"Echidna"','Echidnas use a long tongue to collect small invertebrates.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Echidna','https://www.britannica.com/animal/echidna','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000006','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal includes a short-beaked species whose mother carries its egg in a temporary pouch?','["Horseshoe crab", "Parrotfish", "Koala", "Echidna"]','"Echidna"','A short-beaked echidna incubates its egg in a temporary abdominal pouch.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Echidna','https://www.britannica.com/animal/echidna','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000007','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal has a pouch whose opening faces backward, helping keep out soil while digging?','["Pufferfish", "Kangaroo", "Wombat", "Sea star"]','"Wombat"','A wombat pouch opens toward the rear, reducing entry of soil.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Wombat','https://www.britannica.com/animal/wombat','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000008','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal is a burrowing marsupial with continuously growing incisor teeth?','["Kangaroo", "Wombat", "Sea star", "Pufferfish"]','"Wombat"','Wombats have continuously growing incisors adapted to their abrasive diet.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Wombat','https://www.britannica.com/animal/wombat','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000009','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal has a toughened rump used to help block a burrow entrance against predators?','["Wombat", "Sea star", "Pufferfish", "Kangaroo"]','"Wombat"','A wombat''s reinforced rump provides protection in its burrow.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Wombat','https://www.britannica.com/animal/wombat','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000010','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal can squeeze through small openings because its body has no rigid internal skeleton?','["Sea cucumber", "Shark", "Tasmanian devil", "Octopus"]','"Octopus"','An octopus has no bones; its hard beak is a major limit when squeezing through openings.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Octopus','https://www.britannica.com/animal/octopus','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000011','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal has eight appendages bearing suckers rather than a fish''s fins?','["Shark", "Tasmanian devil", "Octopus", "Sea cucumber"]','"Octopus"','An octopus has eight arms, generally with suckers on their undersides.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Octopus','https://www.britannica.com/animal/octopus','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000012','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal usually releases a dark ink cloud as a defense?','["Tasmanian devil", "Octopus", "Sea cucumber", "Shark"]','"Octopus"','Most octopus species possess an ink sac used in predator defense.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Octopus','https://www.britannica.com/animal/octopus','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000013','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal uses a porous internal cuttlebone to help regulate buoyancy?','["Cuttlefish", "Hagfish", "Narwhal", "Okapi"]','"Cuttlefish"','The cuttlebone contains gas-filled chambers that assist buoyancy.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Cuttlefish','https://www.britannica.com/animal/cuttlefish','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000014','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal commonly has a distinctly W-shaped pupil?','["Hagfish", "Narwhal", "Okapi", "Cuttlefish"]','"Cuttlefish"','Cuttlefish eyes characteristically have W-shaped pupils.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Cuttlefish','https://www.britannica.com/animal/cuttlefish','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000015','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal changes skin patterns using pigment organs called chromatophores?','["Narwhal", "Okapi", "Cuttlefish", "Hagfish"]','"Cuttlefish"','Cuttlefish expand and contract chromatophores to change color patterns.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Cuttlefish','https://www.britannica.com/animal/cuttlefish','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000016','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal lives in the newest chamber of a coiled external shell?','["Giraffe", "Nautilus", "Lamprey", "Beluga"]','"Nautilus"','A nautilus occupies the outermost chamber of its shell.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Nautilus','https://www.britannica.com/animal/nautilus','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000017','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal has an eye resembling a pinhole camera rather than an eye with a lens?','["Nautilus", "Lamprey", "Beluga", "Giraffe"]','"Nautilus"','Nautilus eyes lack the lens present in many other cephalopod eyes.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Nautilus','https://www.britannica.com/animal/nautilus','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000018','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal connects its shell chambers with a tube called a siphuncle?','["Lamprey", "Beluga", "Giraffe", "Nautilus"]','"Nautilus"','The siphuncle links the chambers and participates in buoyancy control.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Nautilus','https://www.britannica.com/animal/nautilus','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000019','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal belongs to the crustacean order Stomatopoda?','["Sperm whale", "Hippopotamus", "Mantis shrimp", "Electric eel"]','"Mantis shrimp"','Mantis shrimps are stomatopod crustaceans, not true shrimps.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Mantis shrimp','https://www.britannica.com/animal/mantis-shrimp','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000020','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal includes species that strike prey with club-like appendages?','["Hippopotamus", "Mantis shrimp", "Electric eel", "Sperm whale"]','"Mantis shrimp"','Smashing mantis shrimps use powerful club-shaped raptorial limbs.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Mantis shrimp','https://www.britannica.com/animal/mantis-shrimp','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000021','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal has species able to detect polarized light?','["Mantis shrimp", "Electric eel", "Sperm whale", "Hippopotamus"]','"Mantis shrimp"','Mantis shrimp eyes can detect polarization as well as color.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Mantis shrimp','https://www.britannica.com/animal/mantis-shrimp','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000022','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal makes a loud snap by rapidly closing one enlarged claw?','["Lungfish", "Sea otter", "Camel", "Pistol shrimp"]','"Pistol shrimp"','Snapping shrimp generate a powerful sound with a specialized large claw.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Pistol shrimp','https://www.britannica.com/animal/snapping-shrimp','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000023','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal creates a collapsing cavitation bubble with its snapping claw?','["Sea otter", "Camel", "Pistol shrimp", "Lungfish"]','"Pistol shrimp"','The claw''s jet forms a bubble whose collapse produces a pressure pulse.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Pistol shrimp','https://www.britannica.com/animal/snapping-shrimp','weird',60),
('41000000-0000-4000-8004-000000000024','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Which animal can share a burrow with a goby that acts as a lookout?','["Camel", "Pistol shrimp", "Lungfish", "Sea otter"]','"Pistol shrimp"','Some pistol shrimps and gobies cooperate: the shrimp maintains the burrow and the goby watches for danger.','Encyclopaedia Britannica: Pistol shrimp','https://www.britannica.com/animal/snapping-shrimp','weird',60),
