('43000000-0000-4000-8003-000000000018','ESTIMATE','A circular garden has radius 4.2 meters. Using pi = 3.1416, estimate its area in square meters. Round to 1 decimal place. Enter only the number.',NULL,'55.4','Area = pi×radius² = 3.1416×4.2² m². Rounded result: 55.4.','Original circular area exercise; worked solution in explanation. OpenStax: underlying mathematical methods','https://openstax.org/books/prealgebra-2e/pages/1-introduction','estimate',60),
('43000000-0000-4000-8003-000000000019','ESTIMATE','A wheel has radius 14.8 centimeters. Using pi = 3.1416, estimate its circumference in centimeters. Round to 1 decimal place. Enter only the number.',NULL,'93.0','Circumference = 2×3.1416×14.8 cm. Rounded result: 93.0.','Original circular circumference exercise; worked solution in explanation. OpenStax: underlying mathematical methods','https://openstax.org/books/prealgebra-2e/pages/1-introduction','estimate',60),
('43000000-0000-4000-8003-000000000020','ESTIMATE','A map scale is 1:50,000. A measured route is 6.8 cm on the map. Estimate actual route length in kilometers. Round to 1 decimal place. Enter only the number.',NULL,'3.4','Each map centimeter represents 50,000 cm = 0.5 km; distance = 6.8×0.5 km. Rounded result: 3.4.','Original map scaling exercise; worked solution in explanation. OpenStax: underlying mathematical methods','https://openstax.org/books/prealgebra-2e/pages/1-introduction','estimate',60),
('43000000-0000-4000-8003-000000000021','ESTIMATE','A parcel weighs 9.2 pounds. Use exactly 1 pound = 0.45359237 kg. Estimate mass in kilograms. Round to 1 decimal place. Enter only the number.',NULL,'4.2','Mass = 9.2×0.45359237 kg. Rounded result: 4.2.','Original unit conversion exercise; worked solution in explanation. OpenStax: underlying mathematical methods','https://openstax.org/books/prealgebra-2e/pages/1-introduction','estimate',60),
('43000000-0000-4000-8003-000000000022','ESTIMATE','A 500-megabyte file downloads at exactly 20 megabits per second. Use 8 bits per byte and decimal units; ignore overhead. Estimate seconds needed. Round to the nearest whole number. Enter only the number.',NULL,'200','Time = file size×8/link rate = 500×8/20 seconds. Rounded result: 200.','Original download time exercise; worked solution in explanation. OpenStax: underlying mathematical methods','https://openstax.org/books/prealgebra-2e/pages/1-introduction','estimate',60),
