('43000000-0000-4000-8003-000000000180','ESTIMATE','A rectangular tank has internal dimensions 110 cm by 90 cm by 35 cm. Estimate capacity in liters; use 1 liter = 1,000 cubic cm. Round to 1 decimal place. Enter only the number.',NULL,'346.5','Capacity = 110×90×35/1000 liters. Rounded result: 346.5.','Original water tank exercise; worked solution in explanation. OpenStax: underlying mathematical methods','https://openstax.org/books/prealgebra-2e/pages/1-introduction','estimate',60),
('43000000-0000-4000-8003-000000000181','ESTIMATE','A tap delivers 13 liters per minute at a constant rate. Estimate minutes to fill an empty 297-liter tank. Round to 1 decimal place. Enter only the number.',NULL,'22.8','Time = volume/flow = 297/13 minutes. Rounded result: 22.8.','Original flow filling exercise; worked solution in explanation. OpenStax: underlying mathematical methods','https://openstax.org/books/prealgebra-2e/pages/1-introduction','estimate',60),
('43000000-0000-4000-8003-000000000182','ESTIMATE','A 385-watt lamp runs for 10 hours. Estimate electricity used in kilowatt-hours. Round to 2 decimal places. Enter only the number.',NULL,'3.85','Energy = power×time = 385/1000×10 kWh. Rounded result: 3.85.','Original electric energy exercise; worked solution in explanation. OpenStax: underlying mathematical methods','https://openstax.org/books/prealgebra-2e/pages/1-introduction','estimate',60),
