('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000009','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Two ropes burn unevenly along their lengths. Rope A takes 72 minutes to burn from one end and rope B takes 66. At time zero light A at both ends and B at one end. As soon as A disappears, light B at its other end. How many minutes after time zero does B disappear?','["51", "52", "50", "53"]','"51"','A finishes after 36 minutes. B then has 30 minutes of one-ended burning left; burning from both ends halves that remainder. Total = 36 + (66-36)/2 = 51. Unevenness of the rope does not affect this timing.','Original uneven-rope timing puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000010','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Two ropes burn unevenly along their lengths. Rope A takes 80 minutes to burn from one end and rope B takes 70. At time zero light A at both ends and B at one end. As soon as A disappears, light B at its other end. How many minutes after time zero does B disappear?','["56", "55", "54", "57"]','"55"','A finishes after 40 minutes. B then has 30 minutes of one-ended burning left; burning from both ends halves that remainder. Total = 40 + (70-40)/2 = 55. Unevenness of the rope does not affect this timing.','Original uneven-rope timing puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000011','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Two ropes burn unevenly along their lengths. Rope A takes 100 minutes to burn from one end and rope B takes 80. At time zero light A at both ends and B at one end. As soon as A disappears, light B at its other end. How many minutes after time zero does B disappear?','["66", "64", "65", "67"]','"65"','A finishes after 50 minutes. B then has 30 minutes of one-ended burning left; burning from both ends halves that remainder. Total = 50 + (80-50)/2 = 65. Unevenness of the rope does not affect this timing.','Original uneven-rope timing puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000012','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You have unmarked 3-litre and 5-litre jugs, initially empty, plus a tap and drain. One action fills a jug, empties a jug, or pours into the other until the source empties or the destination fills. What is the fewest actions to have exactly 4 litres in either jug?','["7", "5", "8", "6"]','"6"','A shortest sequence is: fill the second jug; pour second into first; empty the first jug; pour second into first; fill the second jug; pour second into first. This takes 6 actions. Checking all reachable jug states breadth-first establishes that no shorter sequence reaches the target.','Original water-jug optimization puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000013','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You have unmarked 4-litre and 7-litre jugs, initially empty, plus a tap and drain. One action fills a jug, empties a jug, or pours into the other until the source empties or the destination fills. What is the fewest actions to have exactly 5 litres in either jug?','["8", "9", "7", "10"]','"8"','A shortest sequence is: fill the first jug; pour first into second; fill the first jug; pour first into second; empty the second jug; pour first into second; fill the first jug; pour first into second. This takes 8 actions. Checking all reachable jug states breadth-first establishes that no shorter sequence reaches the target.','Original water-jug optimization puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
