('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000023','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Four people take 1, 2, 5 and 10 minutes to cross a bridge. At most two cross together, at the slower person''s pace. It is dark: every crossing needs the one torch, which must be carried back as needed. All start on the near side. Minimum minutes to get everyone across?','["18", "16", "17", "19"]','"17"','One optimal schedule is out: 1,2; back: 1; out: 5,10; back: 2; out: 1,2, totaling 17 minutes. Enumerating all bank/torch states and selecting the least-cost path proves minimality; a return trip cannot be omitted.','Original bridge-and-torch planning puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
