('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000038','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','17 people must cross a river in one boat carrying at most 5 people. Everybody can row; nobody swims. The boat starts with them, and all people and the boat must finish on the other bank. What is the minimum number of one-way crossings?','["8", "7", "6", "9"]','"7"','Every return carries at least one person. With r returns, there are r+1 outward trips, so at most (r+1)*5-r = 5+r*4 people finish across. Thus r must be at least 3. Send full outward boats and return one rower to attain that bound: 7 crossings.','Original return-trip capacity puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000039','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','20 people must cross a river in one boat carrying at most 4 people. Everybody can row; nobody swims. The boat starts with them, and all people and the boat must finish on the other bank. What is the minimum number of one-way crossings?','["14", "12", "13", "15"]','"13"','Every return carries at least one person. With r returns, there are r+1 outward trips, so at most (r+1)*4-r = 4+r*3 people finish across. Thus r must be at least 6. Send full outward boats and return one rower to attain that bound: 13 crossings.','Original return-trip capacity puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000040','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','23 people must cross a river in one boat carrying at most 6 people. Everybody can row; nobody swims. The boat starts with them, and all people and the boat must finish on the other bank. What is the minimum number of one-way crossings?','["10", "8", "11", "9"]','"9"','Every return carries at least one person. With r returns, there are r+1 outward trips, so at most (r+1)*6-r = 6+r*5 people finish across. Thus r must be at least 4. Send full outward boats and return one rower to attain that bound: 9 crossings.','Original return-trip capacity puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
