('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000044','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','36 people must cross a river in one boat carrying at most 8 people. Everybody can row; nobody swims. The boat starts with them, and all people and the boat must finish on the other bank. What is the minimum number of one-way crossings?','["10", "8", "11", "9"]','"9"','Every return carries at least one person. With r returns, there are r+1 outward trips, so at most (r+1)*8-r = 8+r*7 people finish across. Thus r must be at least 4. Send full outward boats and return one rower to attain that bound: 9 crossings.','Original return-trip capacity puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000045','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You may choose 1 positive-integer weights and put them on either pan of a balance, with the object on one pan. What is the largest N for which your weights can measure every integer object mass from 1 through N?','["1", "2", "0", "3"]','"1"','Choose weights 1,3,9,...,1. Balanced ternary represents every integer up to their sum, 1. Conversely 1 weights have at most 3^1 signed placements; after pairing positive and negative totals, at most (3^1-1)/2 positive masses are available.','Original two-pan weighing insight puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000046','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You may choose 2 positive-integer weights and put them on either pan of a balance, with the object on one pan. What is the largest N for which your weights can measure every integer object mass from 1 through N?','["5", "4", "3", "6"]','"4"','Choose weights 1,3,9,...,3. Balanced ternary represents every integer up to their sum, 4. Conversely 2 weights have at most 3^2 signed placements; after pairing positive and negative totals, at most (3^2-1)/2 positive masses are available.','Original two-pan weighing insight puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
