('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000056','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','An 8 by 8 checkerboard has 1 black squares and 0 white squares removed. Each remaining domino must cover two edge-adjacent squares. Regardless of the hole positions, what is the minimum number of uncovered squares forced by color imbalance alone?','["2", "0", "3", "1"]','"1"','The board starts with 32 of each color. After removal it has 31 black and 32 white squares. Every domino uses one of each, so at least the difference, 1, must remain uncovered. The question asks the color-based lower bound, not whether a particular hole pattern achieves it.','Original checkerboard invariant puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
