('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000067','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','12 doors start shut. On pass k, for every k from 1 through 12, you toggle exactly the doors numbered by multiples of k. How many doors finish open?','["4", "2", "3", "5"]','"3"','Door j is toggled once per divisor of j. Divisors pair except when j is a perfect square; only squares have an odd divisor count. There are floor(sqrt(12)) = 3 squares through 12.','Original divisor-parity doors puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
