('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000100','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A snail starts at the bottom of a 10-metre well. Each day it climbs 3 metres; each night, if still inside, it slides 2 metres. It escapes the moment it reaches the rim. On which day does it escape?','["9", "7", "10", "8"]','"8"','Before day n the snail has gained (n-1)*(3-2) metres. Escape requires that height plus today''s 3-metre climb to reach 10. The least n is 8. There is no slide on the final day.','Original last-day asymmetry puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000101','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A snail starts at the bottom of a 14-metre well. Each day it climbs 5 metres; each night, if still inside, it slides 3 metres. It escapes the moment it reaches the rim. On which day does it escape?','["6", "7", "5", "8"]','"6"','Before day n the snail has gained (n-1)*(5-3) metres. Escape requires that height plus today''s 5-metre climb to reach 14. The least n is 6. There is no slide on the final day.','Original last-day asymmetry puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
