('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000111','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Two cyclists start 90 km apart and ride toward each other at 15 and 30 km/h. A bird flies at 45 km/h, instantly reversing whenever it reaches a cyclist, until the cyclists meet. Ignoring turning time, how far does the bird fly?','["91", "89", "90", "92"]','"90"','The cyclists meet after 90/(15+30) hours. The bird flies continuously for exactly that time, so its distance is 45*90/(15+30) = 90 km. Summing individual zigzags is unnecessary.','Original shared-time shortcut puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
