('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000121','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Two cyclists start 360 km apart and ride toward each other at 40 and 80 km/h. A bird flies at 160 km/h, instantly reversing whenever it reaches a cyclist, until the cyclists meet. Ignoring turning time, how far does the bird fly?','["480", "481", "479", "482"]','"480"','The cyclists meet after 360/(40+80) hours. The bird flies continuously for exactly that time, so its distance is 160*360/(40+80) = 480 km. Summing individual zigzags is unnecessary.','Original shared-time shortcut puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000122','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You start 5-minute and 9-minute hourglasses together. The instant the shorter one empties, you turn it over once. The longer one is not turned. When the longer one first empties, how many minutes of sand remain in the shorter one?','["2", "1", "0", "3"]','"1"','The shorter glass restarts at minute 5. By minute 9, it has run for 4 minutes since its flip. Its remaining time is 5-(9-5) = 1 minutes. Both glasses have uniform flow.','Original hourglass phase tracking puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000123','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You start 6-minute and 10-minute hourglasses together. The instant the shorter one empties, you turn it over once. The longer one is not turned. When the longer one first empties, how many minutes of sand remain in the shorter one?','["3", "1", "2", "4"]','"2"','The shorter glass restarts at minute 6. By minute 10, it has run for 4 minutes since its flip. Its remaining time is 6-(10-6) = 2 minutes. Both glasses have uniform flow.','Original hourglass phase tracking puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000124','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You start 7-minute and 11-minute hourglasses together. The instant the shorter one empties, you turn it over once. The longer one is not turned. When the longer one first empties, how many minutes of sand remain in the shorter one?','["4", "2", "5", "3"]','"3"','The shorter glass restarts at minute 7. By minute 11, it has run for 4 minutes since its flip. Its remaining time is 7-(11-7) = 3 minutes. Both glasses have uniform flow.','Original hourglass phase tracking puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
