('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000133','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Identical machines each finish one item every 4 minutes and begin empty at time zero. A machine works on only one item at a time. All run simultaneously with no setup delay. What is the minimum number of machines needed to finish at least 17 items by minute 9?','["9", "10", "8", "11"]','"9"','One machine can finish floor(9/4) = 2 whole items before the deadline. You therefore need ceil(17/2) = 9 machines. Fractional unfinished batches do not count.','Original parallel batches puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000134','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','Identical machines each finish one item every 5 minutes and begin empty at time zero. A machine works on only one item at a time. All run simultaneously with no setup delay. What is the minimum number of machines needed to finish at least 23 items by minute 16?','["9", "8", "7", "10"]','"8"','One machine can finish floor(16/5) = 3 whole items before the deadline. You therefore need ceil(23/3) = 8 machines. Fractional unfinished batches do not count.','Original parallel batches puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
