('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000144','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A solid convex cake stays fixed in place. You may make 1 straight planar cuts, choosing their angles and positions freely; no pieces are moved or stacked. What is the maximum number of pieces?','["3", "1", "4", "2"]','"2"','For n planes in general position the maximum is 1+n+C(n,2)+C(n,3). A new plane is split by the previous planes into the maximum two-dimensional number of regions, each creating one new piece. With n=1 the total is 2.','Original three-dimensional cutting puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
