('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000155','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','2 volumes stand upright in numerical order left to right, spines facing you. Every page block is 30 mm thick and each cover is 2 mm. Each book''s front cover is on its right and back cover on its left. A worm bores straight from the FIRST page of volume 1 to the LAST page of volume 2. How many millimetres does it travel?','["5", "3", "4", "6"]','"4"','The first page of volume 1 is at its right-hand edge; the last page of volume 2 is at its left-hand edge. The path includes 0 complete interior page blocks and 2 covers, not the outer page blocks. Distance = 0*30 + 2*2 = 4 mm.','Original bookworm orientation puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000156','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','3 volumes stand upright in numerical order left to right, spines facing you. Every page block is 25 mm thick and each cover is 1 mm. Each book''s front cover is on its right and back cover on its left. A worm bores straight from the FIRST page of volume 1 to the LAST page of volume 3. How many millimetres does it travel?','["30", "28", "31", "29"]','"29"','The first page of volume 1 is at its right-hand edge; the last page of volume 3 is at its left-hand edge. The path includes 1 complete interior page blocks and 4 covers, not the outer page blocks. Distance = 1*25 + 4*1 = 29 mm.','Original bookworm orientation puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000157','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','4 volumes stand upright in numerical order left to right, spines facing you. Every page block is 20 mm thick and each cover is 2 mm. Each book''s front cover is on its right and back cover on its left. A worm bores straight from the FIRST page of volume 1 to the LAST page of volume 4. How many millimetres does it travel?','["52", "53", "51", "54"]','"52"','The first page of volume 1 is at its right-hand edge; the last page of volume 4 is at its left-hand edge. The path includes 2 complete interior page blocks and 6 covers, not the outer page blocks. Distance = 2*20 + 6*2 = 52 mm.','Original bookworm orientation puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
