('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000166','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A seven-segment display shows 169. Rotate the entire display by 180 degrees. Use the rule 0->0, 1->1, 2->2, 5->5, 6->9, 8->8, 9->6. Reading the rotated display left to right, which digit string do you see? Preserve leading zeros.','["961", "691", "196", "169"]','"691"','Rotation reverses digit order as well as rotating each individual digit. Reverse 169 and apply the stated mapping to obtain 691.','Original rotated-display reversal puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
