('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000177','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A will leaves 41 indivisible horses to three heirs, specifying shares of 1/2, 1/3 and 1/7. A neighbor lends 1 horses. The heirs apply those shares to the temporary herd, and the neighbor takes back every horse left over. How many horses does the 1/2 heir receive?','["21", "22", "20", "23"]','"21"','The temporary herd has 42 horses. The shares give 21, 14, and 6, totaling 41. Exactly 1 horses remain for the lender. The requested share is 42/2 = 21. This is the explicitly stated borrowing arrangement, not fractional shares of the original herd.','Original temporary-resource inheritance puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000178','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A will leaves 23 indivisible horses to three heirs, specifying shares of 1/2, 1/3 and 1/8. A neighbor lends 1 horses. The heirs apply those shares to the temporary herd, and the neighbor takes back every horse left over. How many horses does the 1/2 heir receive?','["13", "12", "11", "14"]','"12"','The temporary herd has 24 horses. The shares give 12, 8, and 3, totaling 23. Exactly 1 horses remain for the lender. The requested share is 24/2 = 12. This is the explicitly stated borrowing arrangement, not fractional shares of the original herd.','Original temporary-resource inheritance puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000179','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A will leaves 17 indivisible horses to three heirs, specifying shares of 1/2, 1/3 and 1/9. A neighbor lends 1 horses. The heirs apply those shares to the temporary herd, and the neighbor takes back every horse left over. How many horses does the 1/2 heir receive?','["10", "8", "9", "11"]','"9"','The temporary herd has 18 horses. The shares give 9, 6, and 2, totaling 17. Exactly 1 horses remain for the lender. The requested share is 18/2 = 9. This is the explicitly stated borrowing arrangement, not fractional shares of the original herd.','Original temporary-resource inheritance puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
