('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000187','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A will leaves 53 indivisible horses to three heirs, specifying shares of 1/2, 1/3 and 1/20. A neighbor lends 7 horses. The heirs apply those shares to the temporary herd, and the neighbor takes back every horse left over. How many horses does the 1/2 heir receive?','["31", "29", "30", "32"]','"30"','The temporary herd has 60 horses. The shares give 30, 20, and 3, totaling 53. Exactly 7 horses remain for the lender. The requested share is 60/2 = 30. This is the explicitly stated borrowing arrangement, not fractional shares of the original herd.','Original temporary-resource inheritance puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000188','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You travel a fixed distance outward at 12 km/h and return over exactly the same distance. What constant return speed is needed for an average speed of 16 km/h over the whole round trip?','["25", "23", "26", "24"]','"24"','For one-way distance d, total time is d/12+d/v. Set 2d/(d/12+d/v)=16, giving v=16*12/(2*12-16)=24. Equal distances do not imply equal travel times.','Original round-trip average-speed trap puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000189','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You travel a fixed distance outward at 15 km/h and return over exactly the same distance. What constant return speed is needed for an average speed of 20 km/h over the whole round trip?','["30", "31", "29", "32"]','"30"','For one-way distance d, total time is d/15+d/v. Set 2d/(d/15+d/v)=20, giving v=20*15/(2*15-20)=30. Equal distances do not imply equal travel times.','Original round-trip average-speed trap puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000190','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You travel a fixed distance outward at 18 km/h and return over exactly the same distance. What constant return speed is needed for an average speed of 24 km/h over the whole round trip?','["37", "36", "35", "38"]','"36"','For one-way distance d, total time is d/18+d/v. Set 2d/(d/18+d/v)=24, giving v=24*18/(2*18-24)=36. Equal distances do not imply equal travel times.','Original round-trip average-speed trap puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
