('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000198','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','You travel a fixed distance outward at 50 km/h and return over exactly the same distance. What constant return speed is needed for an average speed of 80 km/h over the whole round trip?','["201", "200", "199", "202"]','"200"','For one-way distance d, total time is d/50+d/v. Set 2d/(d/50+d/v)=80, giving v=80*50/(2*50-80)=200. Equal distances do not imply equal travel times.','Original round-trip average-speed trap puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000199','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','3 guests each hand over 10 dollars. The hotel retains 21 dollars, a porter keeps 3, and 6 dollars total are returned to the guests. After the refund, what is the guests'' combined net payment, including the porter''s share?','["25", "23", "24", "26"]','"24"','Net payment is original money minus refund: 30-6=24. It is also hotel plus porter: 21+3=24. Adding the porter''s share to the net payment counts it twice.','Original missing-money bookkeeping puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000200','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','4 guests each hand over 12 dollars. The hotel retains 36 dollars, a porter keeps 4, and 8 dollars total are returned to the guests. After the refund, what is the guests'' combined net payment, including the porter''s share?','["41", "39", "42", "40"]','"40"','Net payment is original money minus refund: 48-8=40. It is also hotel plus porter: 36+4=40. Adding the porter''s share to the net payment counts it twice.','Original missing-money bookkeeping puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
