('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000209','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','13 guests each hand over 25 dollars. The hotel retains 273 dollars, a porter keeps 13, and 39 dollars total are returned to the guests. After the refund, what is the guests'' combined net payment, including the porter''s share?','["286", "287", "285", "288"]','"286"','Net payment is original money minus refund: 325-39=286. It is also hotel plus porter: 273+13=286. Adding the porter''s share to the net payment counts it twice.','Original missing-money bookkeeping puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000210','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A single-elimination tournament starts with 7 entrants. Byes are allowed, and a played match eliminates exactly one entrant. There are no draws or withdrawals, and one champion remains. How many matches must be played?','["7", "6", "5", "8"]','"6"','Every entrant except the champion is eliminated exactly once. That is 7-1=6 eliminations, each requiring one match. Byes change scheduling but eliminate nobody.','Original elimination invariant puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
