('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000221','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A rectangular enclosure has sides 6 and 4 metres. Put fence posts every 2 metres all the way around, with a post at each corner. The spacing divides both side lengths exactly. How many DISTINCT posts are needed?','["10", "11", "9", "12"]','"10"','The perimeter is 2*(6+4)=20 metres, giving 10 spacing intervals. Around a closed loop the last endpoint is the starting post, so the number of distinct posts equals the intervals, not intervals plus one.','Original closed-loop endpoint counting puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
