('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000232','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A train is 100 metres long and moves at 10 metres per second through a 100-metre tunnel. From the instant the front enters until the instant the rear leaves, how many seconds pass?','["21", "19", "22", "20"]','"20"','The front must travel the tunnel length plus the whole train length: 100+100=200 metres. At 10 m/s this takes 20 seconds. Timing only the front''s transit omits the rear''s clearance.','Original moving-extent perspective puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
