('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000243','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A child is 2 years old and their parent is 28. In 2 years, how many times the child''s age will the parent be? Give the exact ratio.','["14", "15", "15/2", "7"]','"15/2"','Both ages increase by 2, becoming 4 and 30. The ratio is (28+2)/(2+2)=15/2. Adding time to only one age, or keeping the current multiplier, gives the wrong ratio.','Original age-difference invariant puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
