('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000251','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A child is 10 years old and their parent is 60. In 10 years, how many times the child''s age will the parent be? Give the exact ratio.','["6", "7", "7/2", "3"]','"7/2"','Both ages increase by 10, becoming 20 and 70. The ratio is (60+10)/(10+10)=7/2. Adding time to only one age, or keeping the current multiplier, gives the wrong ratio.','Original age-difference invariant puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000252','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A child is 11 years old and their parent is 64. In 11 years, how many times the child''s age will the parent be? Give the exact ratio.','["64/11", "75/11", "32/11", "75/22"]','"75/22"','Both ages increase by 11, becoming 22 and 75. The ratio is (64+11)/(11+11)=75/22. Adding time to only one age, or keeping the current multiplier, gives the wrong ratio.','Original age-difference invariant puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000253','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A child is 12 years old and their parent is 68. In 12 years, how many times the child''s age will the parent be? Give the exact ratio.','["10/3", "17/3", "20/3", "17/6"]','"10/3"','Both ages increase by 12, becoming 24 and 80. The ratio is (68+12)/(12+12)=10/3. Adding time to only one age, or keeping the current multiplier, gives the wrong ratio.','Original age-difference invariant puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000254','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A seller serves 1 customers in succession. Each buys half the eggs then present PLUS half an egg. No egg is broken, all purchases are whole numbers, and after the last customer no eggs remain. How many eggs were present before the first sale?','["2", "1", "0", "3"]','"1"','If r whole eggs remain after a sale, the previous count must have been 2r+1. Start with zero and apply that reverse rule 1 times: the initial count is 2^1-1=1. At every step the odd stock count makes the half-plus-half purchase an integer.','Original backward egg-sale reconstruction puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000255','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A seller serves 2 customers in succession. Each buys half the eggs then present PLUS half an egg. No egg is broken, all purchases are whole numbers, and after the last customer no eggs remain. How many eggs were present before the first sale?','["4", "2", "3", "5"]','"3"','If r whole eggs remain after a sale, the previous count must have been 2r+1. Start with zero and apply that reverse rule 2 times: the initial count is 2^2-1=3. At every step the odd stock count makes the half-plus-half purchase an integer.','Original backward egg-sale reconstruction puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000256','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A seller serves 3 customers in succession. Each buys half the eggs then present PLUS half an egg. No egg is broken, all purchases are whole numbers, and after the last customer no eggs remain. How many eggs were present before the first sale?','["8", "6", "9", "7"]','"7"','If r whole eggs remain after a sale, the previous count must have been 2r+1. Start with zero and apply that reverse rule 3 times: the initial count is 2^3-1=7. At every step the odd stock count makes the half-plus-half purchase an integer.','Original backward egg-sale reconstruction puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
