('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000264','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','A seller serves 11 customers in succession. Each buys half the eggs then present PLUS half an egg. No egg is broken, all purchases are whole numbers, and after the last customer no eggs remain. How many eggs were present before the first sale?','["2048", "2046", "2049", "2047"]','"2047"','If r whole eggs remain after a sale, the previous count must have been 2r+1. Start with zero and apply that reverse rule 11 times: the initial count is 2^11-1=2047. At every step the odd stock count makes the half-plus-half purchase an integer.','Original backward egg-sale reconstruction puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000265','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','2 married couples attend a party, including the host and the host''s spouse. No one shakes their own hand or their spouse''s hand, and no pair shakes twice. The host asks each of the other 3 people their handshake total and gets every integer from 0 through 2 exactly once. How many hands did the host''s spouse shake?','["1", "2", "0", "3"]','"1"','The person with 2 shakes met everyone except their spouse, so their spouse must be the person with 0. Remove that couple; the remaining extremes pair in the same way. Repeating leaves the respondent with 1 shakes unpaired, who must be the host''s spouse.','Original spousal handshake pairing puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
('43000000-0000-4000-8001-000000000266','MULTIPLE_CHOICE','3 married couples attend a party, including the host and the host''s spouse. No one shakes their own hand or their spouse''s hand, and no pair shakes twice. The host asks each of the other 5 people their handshake total and gets every integer from 0 through 4 exactly once. How many hands did the host''s spouse shake?','["3", "2", "1", "4"]','"2"','The person with 4 shakes met everyone except their spouse, so their spouse must be the person with 0. Remove that couple; the remaining extremes pair in the same way. Repeating leaves the respondent with 2 shakes unpaired, who must be the host''s spouse.','Original spousal handshake pairing puzzle; worked solution in explanation. Background: Wikipedia Mathematical puzzle','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_puzzle','lateral',180),
